---
import CommunityLayout from '../components/CommunityLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, FEEDBACK_EMAIL } from '../lib/contact';
---

<CommunityLayout
  title="Privacy policy | iDuckImg"
  description="What iDuckImg does and does not do with your pictures and your data. Images are processed in your browser and are not uploaded."
  before="Privacy"
  mark="policy"
  intro="Short version: your pictures stay on your device. Here is the longer version, in plain words."
>
  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="images">
    <h2 id="images" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Your images</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      Every iDuckImg tool opens, changes and saves your pictures inside your own browser. Your images are not uploaded to our
      servers, and we cannot see them or keep a copy. When you close the tab they are gone from the page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="collect">
    <h2 id="collect" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">What we collect</h2>
    <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 leading-relaxed">
      <li>
        <strong>Ordinary web requests.</strong> Our host, Cloudflare, receives the technical details any website receives when a
        page is loaded (such as your IP address, the page asked for and your browser type) and may keep them in standard
        server logs for security and reliability.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your theme choice.</strong> If you pick light or dark mode, it is saved in your browser local storage so the
        site remembers it. It never leaves your device. You can clear it on the <a class="link" href="/settings/">Settings</a>
        page.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Messages you choose to send.</strong> When you press Send on the feedback or request form, your message (and your
        email address, if you typed one) goes through Cloudflare, who host this site, to our inbox ({FEEDBACK_EMAIL}). We use
        Cloudflare Turnstile to tell people from robots; it may look at your browser and IP address for that. We do not keep
        your message on the website or in any database, and the only copy is the email we receive. If you would rather not
        send it that way, you can open it in your own email app or copy it instead. For anything else, write to {CONTACT_EMAIL}.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">We do not have accounts, so we hold no sign-up data. We do not sell personal data.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="ads">
    <h2 id="ads" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Ads and measuring visits</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      iDuckImg may show advertising in the future to cover its costs, and may use a privacy-focused visit counter. If that
      happens, ad and measurement providers may set cookies or collect data about your visit, and where the law requires it we
      will ask for your consent first and update this page before turning them on. Ads are never placed over the area where you
      add or download files, and they never receive your pictures.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="ai">
    <h2 id="ai" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">AI tools</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      iDuckImg has no AI tools today. If we add tools that need your own AI provider key, they will say clearly on the page that
      the picture is sent to that provider, and this page will list which ones.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="rights">
    <h2 id="rights" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight">Your choices and contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
      You can ask what we hold about you, or ask us to delete it, using the <a class="link" href="/feedback/">feedback form</a>.
      Because we keep so little, there is usually nothing beyond server logs. This policy may change; the date below shows when
      it last did.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: 12 November 2026. Operated by Basic App Company.</p>
  </section>
</CommunityLayout>
